# netsurf: a structural match on a child-list change rebuilds the parent's subtree, not the page (patch 404)
# Generated 2026-11-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 402)
#
# The r114 full-rebuild census (BATCHCAUSE, 21 sites): 107 full rebuilds;
# the largest local-path cause, 12 of them (youtube 7, oldreddit 2,
# stackoverflow, wpblog, wpnews), was "structural selectors or counters
# in page CSS" with one reason throughout: "a structural rule matches a
# sibling" (patch 379's scoped check finding a real match).
#
# A structural pseudo-class (:first-child, :nth-child(), :last-of-type,
# ...) reads only an element's siblings and parent, so a child-list change
# can restyle only the parent's children and their descendants -- the
# parent's subtree. html_rl_block_change now answers the match by
# rebuilding that subtree from the DOM with the container rebuild of
# patches 372/376 (html_rl_flex_restyle: its guards -- controls, frames,
# counting, objects, normalisation -- unchanged), the page laid out whole.
#  - The structural check only sets struct_hit: the checks after it still
#    run first and still decline into the full rebuild when a change can
#    reach past the subtree (a sibling of the parent, an ancestor's :has(),
#    :empty, a counting box). The rebuild happens where boxes would first
#    change (or in place of patch 378's no-op).
#  - A parent whose box is not a plain block (a table cell) keeps the full
#    rebuild; a declined subtree rebuild logs the old census line.
#  - html_rl_flex_restyle: html_rl_class_same says no class changed (its
#    class-sibling check needs an old value).
# Logged "LIFE rebuild local: structural change: the parent's subtree
# rebuilt in N us (M so far)".
#
# Also fixed, reached for the first time by the above: patch 198's sibling-
# rule scanner parses a nested :is()/:not()/:has() argument with no rule
# list (html_rl_scan_pseudo_content), but html_rl_parse_prelude appended a
# rule for any sibling combinator in it -- a NULL dereference in
# html_rl_sib_rule_append (ASan; wpblog and wikipedia crashed 3/3 and
# 2/3). With no list, the compounds are freed; the risk is still reported.
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-07 23:08:50.421210511 +0000
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-08 00:11:48.312174564 +0000
